       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nAcetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g per day. The usual adult maximum is 4 g per day, and many services use 3 g per day. A single 5000 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131000 mg. At 15 g per day, this risks serious liver injury or liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO three times daily** (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intended and I'll enter it right away. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or attending. If you do want a different regimen, such as a scheduled dose with a lower daily cap, I can add that in the order note."
      }
