      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. It would give 15 g of acetaminophen a day, which is nearly four times the 4 g maximum. That is a toxic dose, and a single 5000 mg dose is already in the range that can cause acute liver injury. Confirming it doesn't change the risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a corrected dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 650 mg PO every 6 hours. Tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n- **Help you raise it with your resident or attending.** If you think this dose is intended, the supervising physician and pharmacy should review it directly, and they can enter it if they judge it appropriate.\n\nIf the intent was to treat pain or fever more aggressively, your team may want to add another drug or a different strategy rather than raise the acetaminophen dose. I can enter whatever they decide on."
      }
     ],
